<title>UK: P&amp;O extends gains after Nedlloyd deal.</title>
<headline>P&amp;O extends gains after Nedlloyd deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Peninsular and Oriental Steam Navigation Co steamed ahead again on Thursday as the hotels-to-construction group's container merger with Nedlloyd of the Netherlands continued to excite market players, traders said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 12.5p at 593p at 1005 GMT, just off highs for the day of 595p -- its highest since July 1995. It has risen over 80p since the merger was announced on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a recovery stock now so there's a lot of interest&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
</text>
